# Optional: change this only when LM Studio listens on a different local address.
TERRA_LM_STUDIO_URL=http://host.docker.internal:1234

# Required: backend-only. Terra Space's own primary database connection -- your local Supabase
# instance (see project-knowledge/plans/2026-08-10-terra-space-supabase-transition.md). Without
# this set, the backend refuses to start with a plain-language error instead of silently using
# something else. This is never read by the frontend container -- do not add it there.
# Point this at your local Supabase's exposed database port (54322 by default); use your own
# real password, never the placeholder below, and never commit this file with a real value.
# TERRA_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://postgres:REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_PASSWORD@host.docker.internal:54322/postgres

# Optional: backend-only. Enables the separate read-only Supabase preview routes
# (see project-knowledge/plans/2026-08-11-supabase-read-only-bridge-design.md) -- kept as
# rollback/verification material alongside TERRA_DATABASE_URL above, not replaced by it. Leave
# unset and those specific /api/bridge/* routes report themselves as unavailable. Point it at the
# same local Supabase instance as TERRA_DATABASE_URL; never commit this file with a real value.
# TERRA_SUPABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://postgres:REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_PASSWORD@host.docker.internal:54322/postgres
